data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O on the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed** — no opt-in exists anymore. In .NET 10 you could re-enable it; in EF Core 11, all synchronous calls (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`) **always throw**.

### Fix: convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

All callers of these methods must be updated to `await` the results as well. There is no workaround — the Cosmos SDK is async-only, and EF Core 11 no longer bridges the gap.

**Bonus:** If your entities have owned collections, also note that empty owned collections now return an empty collection instead of `null` (update any `is null` checks to `.Count == 0`).
